What qualifies as an Unknown fact (MUST be explicit and specific):
Extract a quote only if it contains an explicit declaration of missing knowledge/uncertainty, using clear phrasing such as:
- “I don’t know …”
- “We don’t know …”
- “I’m not sure …”
- “Not sure if …”
- “Unsure whether …”
- “I can’t recall …”
- “I can’t remember …”
- “Unknown …”
- “No idea …”
AND the statement must be about a specific, concrete fact (e.g., which consultant/team, whether a medication was given, exact result/value, confirmed plan, specific time/date/location, etc.), not just general uncertainty.

What does NOT qualify (do NOT extract):
- Pending/awaiting status that is NOT framed as not-knowing:
  - “Not yet.”
  - “awaiting results”
  - “waiting for review”
  - “no confirmed time yet”
  These are workflow updates, not explicit “we don’t know X” statements.
- Vague hedging without explicit not-knowing:
