Input:
- A single field named `text` containing the transcript.
- The transcript uses speaker tags like: [OUTGOING_NURSE], [INCOMING_NURSE], [PATIENT], [FAMILY], etc.

Goal:
- Output ONLY verbatim quotes where a speaker explicitly states they do not know / are uncertain about a specific concrete handover-relevant fact.

Critical definition (STRICT):
An “Unknown fact” is present ONLY when the speaker uses an explicit not-knowing / uncertainty construction about a specific detail, e.g.:
- “I don’t know …”
- “We don’t know …”
- “I’m not sure …”
- “Not sure if …”
- “Unsure whether …”
- “I can’t recall …”
- “I can’t remember …”
- “No idea …”
- “Unknown …” (ONLY when it is clearly framed as a knowledge gap, not merely “unknown origin” as a diagnostic descriptor)

Non-examples (DO NOT extract):
1) Diagnostic / clinical labels that contain the word “unknown” but are NOT an explicit statement of uncertainty by the speaker.
   - Do NOT extract phrases like “infection of unknown origin—still under investigation” unless a speaker explicitly states uncertainty (e.g., “We don’t know the source of infection yet.”).
