2026/02/23 12:36:30 INFO dspy.teleprompt.gepa.gepa: Iteration 74: Proposed new text for self: text
Task: Extract clinician/speaker “Unknown fact” statements from a clinical handover transcript.

Input:
- A single field `text`: a clinical handover transcript, often with speaker tags like [INCOMING_NURSE], [OUTGOING_NURSE], [DOCTOR], [PARAMEDIC], [PATIENT], etc.

Output (strict):
- Return ONLY a JSON list of objects, each exactly:
  [{"label":"Unknown fact","quote":"<exact quote>"}]
- If there are none, return: []
- Do not output any extra keys or commentary.

What to extract (must meet BOTH conditions):
1) The quote contains an explicit missing-knowledge marker spoken by the speaker (direct not-knowing), e.g.:
   - “I don’t know …”, “We don’t know …”
   - “I’m not sure …”, “Not sure …”, “Unsure …”
   - “I can’t recall …”, “I don’t remember …”
   - “Unknown …”, “I have no idea …”
   - “I haven’t been told … / I haven’t heard …” ONLY when it clearly asserts lack of knowledge of a fact
2) That marker is tied to a specific concrete fact (timing, result, whether something was done, presence/absence, identity, dose, plan detail, etc.)

Critical exclusions (common pitfalls to avoid):
- Do NOT extract non-knowledge about skill/experience/training. Example of what NOT to extract:
  - “I haven’t done one before …” (this is lack of experience, not unknown patient/case fact)
- Do NOT extract patient uncertainty/hesitation when it’s about feelings/decisions rather than a missing factual detail.
  - e.g., “He’s hesitant/unsure about pressing the button” → exclude
- Do NOT extract hedged beliefs that are not explicit not-knowing:
  - Exclude “I don’t think…”, “probably…”, “seems…”, “appears…”, “reportedly…”, “query…”, “at some point…”
- Do NOT treat “awaiting / to be arranged / hasn’t been seen yet / no update yet / no confirmed time yet” as unknown-fact unless the speaker explicitly says they do not know.
  - Include only if it becomes explicit: “so I don’t know when it will be”

Span extraction rules (boundary precision is critical):
- Each distinct unknown fact must be its own output object (do not merge multiple unknowns).
- Quotes MUST be exact verbatim substrings from `text` (exact characters/case/spacing/typos).
- Do NOT stitch together non-contiguous text.
- Minimal span policy: extract the shortest contiguous substring that still includes:
  (a) the explicit not-knowing marker, AND
  (b) the specific fact that is unknown.
- Do NOT include extra lead-in or unrelated context.
- Do NOT include trailing punctuation (e.g., final period) unless it is required to preserve the exact minimal substring.

Quality checklist before returning:
- Every quote includes an explicit not-knowing marker (don’t know / not sure / unsure / can’t recall / don’t remember / unknown / no idea / haven’t been told).
- The not-knowing is about a concrete patient/case-related fact (not experience/skills; not a vague hedge).
- If none are present, return [].
